.he "yacc (1)                     8/18/26                      yacc (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
yacc
- yet another compiler-compiler
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
yacc [ -vrd ] grammar
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Yacc converts a context-free grammar into a set of tables for a simple
automaton which executes an LR(1) parsing algorithm.  The grammar may
be ambiguous; specified precedence rules are used to break ambiguities.
.sp
The output is y.tab.c, which must be compiled by the C compiler and
loaded with any other routines required, perhaps a lexical analyzer,
and the yacc library:
.nf
	cc y.tab.c other.o -ly
.fi
.sp
If the -v flag is given, the file y.output is prepared, containing a
description of the parsing tables and a report on conflicts generated
by ambiguities in the grammar.
.sp
The -r flag causes yacc to accept grammars with Ratfor actions and
produce Ratfor output on y.tab.r.
.sp
If the -d flag is used, the file y.tab.h is generated with the define
statements that associate the yacc-assigned token codes with the
user-declared token names.  This allows source files other than y.tab.c
to access the token codes.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
FILES
.in +5
.br
.nf
	y.output	description of the parsing tables, with -v
	y.tab.c		the C parser
	y.tab.r		the Ratfor parser, with -r
	y.tab.h		defines for token names, with -d
	yacc.tmp, yacc.acts
			temporary files
	/lib/liby.a	runtime library
	/usr/lib/yaccopar
			parser prototype for C programs
	/usr/lib/yaccepar
			parser prototype for EFL programs
	/usr/lib/yaccrpar
			parser prototype for Ratfor programs
.fi
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
lex (1)
.sp
Yacc - Yet Another Compiler Compiler, by S. C. Johnson.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DIAGNOSTICS
.in +5
.br
The number of reduce-reduce and shift-reduce conflicts is reported on
the standard output; a more detailed report is found in the y.output
file.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
BUGS
.in +5
.br
Because file names are fixed, at most one yacc process can be active in
a given directory at a time.
